										Sketch the ellipse <m>\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+ \dfrac{y^2}{b^2} = 1</m>, labelling the coordinates of the points where it crosses the <m>x</m>-axis and the <m>y</m>-axis. Prove that the area of this ellipse is <m>\pi ab</m>.
									</p>
        </statement>
      </exercise><exercise>
